    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="1016" n="920" xml:id="pg920"/>

                <head>No. 426.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoffman to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-05-13"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 13, 1879</date>.
                        (Received May 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 102.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that several
                    cases of cattle disease (<hi rendition="#italic">peste bovine</hi>) have
                    appeared at St. Petersburg, and that active measures have been taken to stamp it
                    out. Orders have been issued: <list>
                        <label>1st.</label>
                        <item>To kill all animals infected or supposed to be infected, paying the
                            owners therefor.</item>
                        <label>2d.</label>
                        <item>Forbidding the cattle at St. Petersburg to be allowed to graze in
                            common.</item>
                        <label>3d.</label>
                        <item>Establishing a strict veterinary inspection in all parts of the city
                            where the disease has already made, or may hereafter make, its
                            appearance.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Some thirty cases have been reported thus far.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WICKHAM HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
